<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Simulation 101, lesson 5.3: a store as a library (PRO: SharedState, declare + Import).

  The store of lesson 5.2 with a different supply side: it does not order from the outside world, it asks a warehouse. One row is one day.
    cell stock   units on the shelf at the end of the day
    cell rcv     units that arrive at the start of the next day (the library clears it every row; the importing model adds the shipment)
    cell req     the request sent to the warehouse (Q units, or 0), written by the store's policy
    cell dem     the day's demand, written by the importing model (the store has customers, but they live outside the library)
    cell lost, seen   the day's lost units and the demand the store saw (written so the day's numbers go through the same door)
  Policy: if stock + rcv + req <= R, request Q.  The three terms are the shelf, the shipment arriving now and the request the warehouse is still filling.
  Sales:  stock := max(0, stock + rcv - dem); lost := max(0, dem - stock - rcv).
  Lost sales. A shortfall at the warehouse is never made up: a request is filled in full, in part, or not at all, and what is not shipped is not owed.

  Declared parameters (overridable per Import; a declare replaces a whole attribute value, so R and Q travel as Constant columns and the
  cells string is declared as a whole):   R (default 32)   Q (default 12)   cells (default "stock=40, rcv=0, req=0, dem=0, lost=0, seen=0")

  Run on its own the store has no customers and no supplier: every row is the same (nothing sells, nothing is requested, the shelf stays at 40).
  Its use is to be imported: samples/pro/inventory-warehouse.xml imports it twice.
  Output columns: 0 stock at the end of the day, 1 units lost today, 2 the demand the store saw today, 3 the request it sent today.
  Lead time, counted from the end of the day the policy looked at: 3 days (one for the policy's read, one for the warehouse's read, one in the shipment's cell).
  14 nodes.
-->
<dataset columns="stock, lost, demand, request">
  <root node="Day"/>
  <definitions>
    <declare name="cells" value="stock=40, rcv=0, req=0, dem=0, lost=0, seen=0"/>
    <declare name="R" value="32"/>
    <declare name="Q" value="12"/>
  </definitions>
  <nodes>
    <SharedState name="Store" cells="$cells"/>
    <StateRead name="ShelfForPolicy" collaborate.state="Store" cells="stock, rcv, req"/>
    <Constant name="Rcol" value="$R" type="double"/>
    <Constant name="Qcol" value="$Q" type="double"/>
    <Append name="PolicyIn">
      <input name="ShelfForPolicy"/>
      <input name="Rcol"/>
      <input name="Qcol"/>
    </Append>
    <Calculate name="Policy" dimension="1" expression="y[0] = if(x[0] + x[1] + x[2] &lt;= x[3], x[4], 0)">
      <input name="PolicyIn"/>
    </Calculate>
    <StateWrite name="PlaceRequest" collaborate.state="Store" cells="req" mode="set">
      <input name="Policy"/>
    </StateWrite>
    <StateRead name="ShelfForSales" collaborate.state="Store" cells="stock, rcv, dem"/>
    <Calculate name="Sales" dimension="3"
               expression="y[0] = max(0, x[0] + x[1] - x[2]); y[1] = max(0, x[2] - x[0] - x[1]); y[2] = x[2]">
      <input name="ShelfForSales"/>
    </Calculate>
    <StateWrite name="Close" collaborate.state="Store" cells="stock, lost, seen" mode="set">
      <input name="Sales"/>
    </StateWrite>
    <Constant name="Zero" value="0" type="double"/>
    <StateWrite name="ClearReceipts" collaborate.state="Store" cells="rcv" mode="set">
      <input name="Zero"/>
    </StateWrite>
    <Append name="Pair">
      <input name="Close"/>
      <input name="PlaceRequest"/>
      <input name="ClearReceipts"/>
    </Append>
    <Arrange name="Day" columns="0,1,2,3">
      <input name="Pair"/>
    </Arrange>
  </nodes>
</dataset>
